TAKEAWAY
  NO BACKPRESSURE : overflow, data is lost.
  LATE BACKPRESSURE: a stall that is only raised when the FIFO is full still overflows;
                     the signal latency must be covered by headroom (watermarks) or credits.
  TOO MUCH CAUTION: too few credits (or a watermark that is too low) never loses data but
                     starves the consumer. Size the buffer for the round-trip latency:
                     capacity >= flow-control latency + items needed to keep the consumer busy.

